WEBVTT

01:49.359 --> 01:51.694
"He suffered a pathetic defeat

01:51.778 --> 01:56.282
because he went out to find Pickle
unprepared to fight and without purpose."

01:56.366 --> 02:00.787
"Although he's my son,
I'm disgusted by his lack of prudence."

02:01.871 --> 02:04.290
That's going a bit far, don't you think?

02:04.874 --> 02:07.168
Baki did what he could.

02:08.002 --> 02:11.256
Has the head
of the Tokugawa Conglomerate gone senile?

02:12.966 --> 02:17.595
"I'll try hard. I'll do my very best.
I'll do my utmost."

02:18.096 --> 02:20.306
Those are all the words of a loser.

02:21.182 --> 02:24.060
There's a world
where none of that matters.

02:24.894 --> 02:27.147
You're spouting out stuff you learned

02:27.230 --> 02:29.149
way back when you were younger.

02:30.191 --> 02:34.028
If you ever try to be
evasive with me again,

02:35.113 --> 02:37.073
that'll be it for you, gramps.

02:37.157 --> 02:39.159
Oh, I...

02:40.368 --> 02:41.327
I'm sorry.

02:43.288 --> 02:46.082
Gramps, how lucky we are.

02:46.916 --> 02:48.084
Huh?

02:48.168 --> 02:51.296
The fact is,
he's now encountered that savage.

02:52.046 --> 02:56.092
That bastard, I bet he won't
be able to sleep for a long time.

02:56.676 --> 02:59.596
I bet that's what he's saying.

03:00.180 --> 03:02.348
"That damn fool!"

03:02.974 --> 03:05.435
<i>I won't be able to sleep for a while.</i>

03:08.938 --> 03:12.609
<i>That alone gave me plenty to enjoy.</i>

03:13.568 --> 03:15.111
<i>I can tell what he is,</i>

03:15.737 --> 03:17.614
<i>how great he is.</i>

03:18.573 --> 03:21.117
<i>With that single blow, we're buddies.</i>

03:24.913 --> 03:26.122
<i>Can I surpass it?</i>

03:32.754 --> 03:34.130
<i>That level...</i>

03:35.215 --> 03:40.511
<i>That level that I knew
I could never achieve the way I am now...</i>

03:41.721 --> 03:43.139
<i>But with him,</i>

03:44.140 --> 03:45.266
<i>I can surpass it!</i>

03:45.975 --> 03:47.894
SHINSHINKAI HEADQUARTERS

03:49.479 --> 03:54.400
I'm pretty sure it was done like this.
The so-called "Mach Punch."

03:55.026 --> 03:58.613
It's the only move of yours
that's ever surprised me.

04:00.490 --> 04:03.743
The power generated
by your big toes in two places

04:03.826 --> 04:05.411
is accelerated by your ankles.

04:05.995 --> 04:08.289
It's further accelerated by both knees.

04:09.290 --> 04:11.209
And by your hips and lumbars.

04:12.126 --> 04:15.421
It's accelerated by your spine,
and then your shoulders.

04:16.005 --> 04:19.175
Followed by your elbows, then your wrists.

04:19.968 --> 04:21.928
Then your fist.

04:23.137 --> 04:26.933
<i>I saw you use this move once
when fighting Hanayama.</i>

04:28.601 --> 04:29.519
I'll be honest.

04:30.019 --> 04:32.313
It sent a chill up my spine.

04:32.939 --> 04:34.524
This is what I said then.

04:35.775 --> 04:41.281
We surpassed where you are now
2,000 years ago!

04:42.573 --> 04:44.200
That was no lie.

04:44.784 --> 04:45.952
But the truth is,

04:46.703 --> 04:49.580
I have only performed it in practice.

04:50.373 --> 04:52.458
I've never used it in real life.

04:53.293 --> 04:56.212
<i>I achieved victory
with the martial arts I've cultivated.</i>

04:56.796 --> 05:00.967
But after that fight, it's apparent
there is no difference in our strength.

05:02.218 --> 05:04.971
In the long history of kung fu,

05:05.596 --> 05:11.060
I believe there is only one
who has ever mastered this move.

05:11.811 --> 05:15.315
Katsumi, you should hone this move

05:16.441 --> 05:17.984
and make it ever quicker!

05:18.609 --> 05:21.237
Put it in the hands of your natural gift!

05:22.363 --> 05:25.450
That's 140 dozen barrels of chloroform,

05:25.533 --> 05:30.038
which is 1.5 times the weight of air.

05:30.121 --> 05:32.790
We took him by surprise
and poured in the liquid,

05:32.874 --> 05:35.501
successfully putting him to sleep.

05:35.585 --> 05:39.672
This was only possible
because he returned here on his own.

05:39.756 --> 05:43.009
We urgently need to build a facility
that can properly contain him.

05:43.634 --> 05:46.179
We must not forget our incredible fortune

05:46.262 --> 05:49.015
in encountering the miraculous specimen
that is Pickle.

05:49.098 --> 05:51.684
We have a responsibility.

05:51.768 --> 05:54.520
Since we found him,
he is now our responsibility.

05:55.229 --> 06:00.276
Without a doubt,
he is a Super-Class-A research specimen,

06:00.360 --> 06:02.779
but he's not a guinea pig.

06:02.862 --> 06:06.115
He is a human being with a personality.

06:06.616 --> 06:10.995
I'm not so sure we should treat him as if
he were some kind of research sample.

06:11.079 --> 06:13.664
"So we should have him fight."

06:13.748 --> 06:15.792
Is that what you're telling me?

06:17.168 --> 06:20.505
There's no need for a facility
to lock Pickle up.

06:21.631 --> 06:24.300
He won't leave here.

06:25.134 --> 06:27.303
<i>After he kicked Baki,</i>

06:27.387 --> 06:31.057
<i>during the few hours before he was put
to sleep with the chloroform,</i>

06:31.140 --> 06:34.060
<i>he didn't make a single move to leave.</i>

06:35.103 --> 06:38.523
Even though he has the strength
to burst down a steel door,

06:38.606 --> 06:41.818
he stayed here of his own accord.

06:46.447 --> 06:47.824
He realizes now

06:47.907 --> 06:50.827
<i>that this is an oasis.</i>

06:50.910 --> 06:55.832
As long as he stays here,
he'll never run out of food or companions.

06:57.083 --> 06:58.334
I'll even swear to it.

06:58.418 --> 07:01.838
When Pickle wakes up,
he won't try to escape.

07:01.921 --> 07:05.550
No need for those guards. He won't run.

07:05.633 --> 07:06.843
Agreed.

07:07.760 --> 07:08.594
Hey.

07:24.694 --> 07:26.362
He's yawning.

07:33.953 --> 07:35.913
He's searching

07:36.956 --> 07:39.375
for food or someone to play with.

07:39.459 --> 07:40.626
That's ridiculous!

07:41.502 --> 07:43.129
Pickle!

07:45.965 --> 07:49.635
Wait just a little longer
for food and a friend.

07:49.719 --> 07:53.139
You can go back to sleep.

07:53.222 --> 07:56.642
Do you really think he understands you?

08:07.236 --> 08:09.655
Pretty much what I expected.

08:09.739 --> 08:10.698
Agreed.

08:21.000 --> 08:25.338
<i>Before, I could never hide
a single page of a newspaper.</i>

08:26.005 --> 08:29.175
<i>But now,
I can hide it completely in my fist.</i>

08:32.512 --> 08:34.347
<i>Next time, I'll let this power loose</i>

08:35.014 --> 08:37.058
<i>with everything I've got.</i>

08:37.642 --> 08:39.685
<i>On Pickle, obviously.</i>

08:41.771 --> 08:42.605
That's it!

08:43.773 --> 08:46.192
This is it. That line.

08:46.275 --> 08:47.735
That's the shockwave.

08:48.277 --> 08:52.657
It's the wave from a bullet,
a jet airplane, or a gunpowder explosion.

08:52.740 --> 08:54.951
It indicates
that Mach speed has been passed.

08:55.618 --> 08:59.455
<i>Only gunpowder or jet engines
can achieve that supersonic speed.</i>

08:59.539 --> 09:01.457
But there is one tool that can achieve

09:01.541 --> 09:04.460
that amazing speed with just human power.

09:06.837 --> 09:07.797
This.

09:08.381 --> 09:09.215
A whip.

09:10.383 --> 09:13.970
If you use this leather rope just right,

09:15.471 --> 09:18.349
the tip can break Mach speed.

09:24.313 --> 09:25.731
Woo-hoo! Awesome!

09:26.315 --> 09:28.276
You only flung it in the air.

09:28.901 --> 09:30.319
It didn't hit anything.

09:31.320 --> 09:33.447
Even so, it made a deafening crack.

09:34.073 --> 09:36.242
The sound signals supersonic speed.

09:37.785 --> 09:38.744
This!

09:38.828 --> 09:41.330
Whoa, I'm surprised they filmed this.

09:41.831 --> 09:45.251
A high-speed camera
captured the tip of the whip.

09:46.085 --> 09:51.257
The widening circle it makes at the moment
it breaks Mach speed is the shockwave.

09:52.466 --> 09:54.260
Starting in the big toes,

09:54.343 --> 09:57.221
by fully using all ten joints,

09:57.305 --> 09:59.765
you can surpass Mach speed.

10:00.349 --> 10:03.185
Mach speed is 1,225 kph.

10:03.269 --> 10:07.356
Therefore, each joint must twist
faster than 100 kph.

10:08.524 --> 10:09.775
It's impossible.

10:10.359 --> 10:13.529
Yes. There are too few joints.

10:13.613 --> 10:16.782
Yes, there are too few.
Then how can we achieve it?

10:18.618 --> 10:21.454
<i>With the backbone. The spine.</i>

10:21.537 --> 10:22.955
<i>That's right.</i>

10:23.039 --> 10:26.042
<i>The backbone is made up of 31 bone joints.</i>

10:26.834 --> 10:31.047
<i>Among them, due to their function,
17 joints can accelerate simultaneously.</i>

10:31.922 --> 10:34.300
That's a total of 27 points of movement.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.802
Mach speed can be broken!

10:45.686 --> 10:48.731
But Master Retsu, will this be enough?

10:49.523 --> 10:53.819
Do you think it can pierce
that super-male's thick muscle tissue?

10:54.737 --> 10:58.532
Do you really think that his rivals
weren't stronger than this?

10:59.200 --> 11:00.868
Naturally, it will not be enough.

11:04.121 --> 11:05.331
That's what I figured.

11:06.040 --> 11:09.168
Katsumi, this move
has even more potential.

11:09.710 --> 11:14.340
There is potential for adding
even more speed and weight to your fist.

11:14.965 --> 11:18.344
From here. And from here.

11:18.427 --> 11:20.554
And here.

11:22.181 --> 11:24.058
You can produce even more speed

11:24.141 --> 11:27.853
by thrusting with the first
through the third joints of the fingers.

11:27.937 --> 11:33.859
If that's not enough, and you want to add
weight to that high speed, then use this.

11:34.819 --> 11:37.363
Use your mind? No, not that.

11:40.199 --> 11:43.202
<i>The heaviest part
of the human body, the head.</i>

11:43.285 --> 11:44.870
<i>By making full use of it,</i>

11:44.954 --> 11:48.040
<i>the weight of the head
can be added to a piercing</i> nukite.

11:48.124 --> 11:50.835
<i>It's the most perfect weapon
in karate history.</i>

11:50.918 --> 11:52.628
<i>It can be achieved.</i>

11:54.004 --> 11:58.801
Now I understand
why you were called "Lethal Weapon."

12:01.011 --> 12:04.724
<i>Once, a certain Japanese man
traveled to China.</i>

12:05.599 --> 12:09.353
<i>He fought numerous matches
against many martial artists,</i>

12:09.937 --> 12:12.148
<i>and was victorious every time.</i>

12:13.274 --> 12:14.900
<i>That was Doppo Orochi.</i>

12:16.277 --> 12:20.281
<i>When Doppo returned to Japan,
he purchased a child from the circus.</i>

12:20.364 --> 12:23.200
<i>Intimidated by skill
that surpassed his own,</i>

12:23.284 --> 12:27.204
<i>Doppo paid a huge sum
and made the boy his ally.</i>

12:28.497 --> 12:29.957
My dad is awful.

12:30.040 --> 12:33.335
There is such a fairy tale
in my own country.

12:34.003 --> 12:36.255
But when I look at you now,

12:36.338 --> 12:39.300
I see that it is not entirely a lie.

12:40.551 --> 12:42.970
It is true,
up to the part about the circus.

12:43.721 --> 12:46.515
If my dad, Doppo Orochi,
was that much of a softie,

12:46.599 --> 12:48.726
I would have had a pretty easy life.

12:50.352 --> 12:51.729
You have achieved it.

12:52.897 --> 12:55.483
Onto the blade unique to karate
known as "nukite,"

12:55.566 --> 12:59.987
you have added the heaviest part
of the human body, the head.

13:00.738 --> 13:04.283
<i>Put differently, it's like a saber
with the weight of an axe.</i>

13:04.784 --> 13:07.495
<i>In other words, you've obtained
an unobtainable weapon.</i>

13:08.370 --> 13:11.248
You'll strike this perfect weapon
at supersonic speed.

13:15.920 --> 13:16.754
Huh?

13:17.421 --> 13:18.506
What?!

13:18.589 --> 13:20.508
Master Kaku!

13:20.591 --> 13:22.218
When did you arrive in Japan?

13:22.301 --> 13:27.056
If you had contacted me,
I would have met you at the airport.

13:29.183 --> 13:31.644
I didn't think you'd arrive so quickly.

13:31.727 --> 13:32.937
Uh, um...

13:34.772 --> 13:36.524
This is Sea Emperor Kaku.

13:36.607 --> 13:39.276
When it comes to kung fu, he's the man.

13:40.236 --> 13:42.363
He is 146 years old.

13:42.446 --> 13:43.531
A hundred...

13:44.114 --> 13:47.409
Based not on his past career,
but on his skill,

13:47.493 --> 13:50.871
he is the reigning master of kung fu.

13:51.872 --> 13:52.748
Sir!

13:56.377 --> 14:01.006
I heard that the Japanese
were a humble people,

14:01.090 --> 14:03.801
but they are far more humble
than I expected.

14:05.970 --> 14:06.804
Bam!

14:07.805 --> 14:14.061
Crowning that move with the word "perfect"
seems to show a lack of greed to me.

14:14.979 --> 14:17.565
Were you watching, Master?

14:17.648 --> 14:20.317
I've been watching this whole time.

14:20.401 --> 14:22.611
I heard everything you said too.

14:24.488 --> 14:25.364
Master...

14:25.906 --> 14:28.576
Then, what is it you... Oh!

14:29.159 --> 14:33.080
Is there really anything
that is "perfect" in this world?

14:33.789 --> 14:35.583
Yes, there is.

14:38.669 --> 14:41.338
Is this what you want?

14:41.422 --> 14:44.091
Yes. Watch very carefully.

14:44.174 --> 14:47.344
This is... the perfect move.

15:00.190 --> 15:01.525
Dang, that's cool.

15:02.443 --> 15:06.113
That's not just a total of 27 joints.

15:06.780 --> 15:10.993
If you want to accelerate a move,
any number of joints can be added.

15:11.076 --> 15:14.496
One hundred, a thousand,
any number you like.

15:23.422 --> 15:24.256
<i>Listen,</i>

15:25.174 --> 15:30.262
forget 27 joints, all I need are the ones
from my shoulder to my fingertips.

15:30.846 --> 15:34.558
There are only a few joints,
but I achieved supersonic speed.

15:34.642 --> 15:36.185
Amazing, isn't it?

15:37.478 --> 15:41.148
In reality, I've used only a few joints.

15:41.815 --> 15:44.526
But the truth is quite different.

15:45.110 --> 15:47.321
<i>Regardless of its actual structure,</i>

15:47.404 --> 15:51.283
<i>the way I imagine it is different.
The imagination knows no limits.</i>

15:52.159 --> 15:54.787
Do you understand, Japanese samurai?

15:56.080 --> 15:58.290
<i>The imagination knows no limits.</i>

16:02.378 --> 16:03.879
<i>Joints</i>

16:04.880 --> 16:06.715
<i>that don't exist...</i>

16:07.383 --> 16:08.801
<i>Increase...</i>

16:11.428 --> 16:12.346
<i>the joints...</i>

16:13.389 --> 16:15.224
<i>Imagine.</i>

16:15.307 --> 16:17.601
<i>The actual structure is like this.</i>

16:17.685 --> 16:19.311
<i>So maybe like this?</i>

16:19.395 --> 16:20.604
<i>Or maybe like this?</i>

16:21.146 --> 16:23.565
<i>No. That's ridiculous.</i>

16:23.649 --> 16:25.985
<i>How am I supposed to believe that?</i>

16:26.068 --> 16:29.071
<i>There's no way the imagination
can overcome reality.</i>

16:29.655 --> 16:30.698
<i>The egg...</i>

16:30.781 --> 16:34.076
<i>For what reason is the egg
a body surrounded by a shell?</i>

16:34.660 --> 16:36.578
<i>It goes without saying.</i>

16:36.662 --> 16:38.580
<i>It is to protect the frail body.</i>

16:39.456 --> 16:40.332
<i>That's it.</i>

16:40.416 --> 16:43.085
<i>It desired a strong shell. Right!</i>

16:44.545 --> 16:47.715
<i>For example, those tree leaves
that grow far above its head.</i>

16:47.798 --> 16:49.717
<i>"I want to eat those leaves."</i>

16:49.800 --> 16:52.386
<i>By wishing that,
the giraffe stretched its neck</i>.

16:52.886 --> 16:54.722
<i>The elephant stretched its trunk.</i>

16:54.805 --> 16:57.474
<i>That's right. They did it to survive!</i>

16:58.142 --> 16:59.935
<i>The stripes on the zebra.</i>

17:00.019 --> 17:03.480
<i>The stripes on the tiger.
The spots on the leopard.</i>

17:03.564 --> 17:07.568
<i>The mimicry of the insects.
Birds' wings. The cobra's poison.</i>

17:07.651 --> 17:09.862
<i>They're all for their survival.</i>

17:13.282 --> 17:16.201
<i>It was the animals' tenacity for life.</i>

17:17.036 --> 17:20.122
<i>Thanks to that, they achieved
incredible evolutionary changes.</i>

17:20.873 --> 17:23.375
<i>Compared to what they obtained,</i>

17:23.459 --> 17:26.003
<i>the body modifications used for battle...</i>

17:26.086 --> 17:28.130
<i>They're so modest.</i>

17:28.213 --> 17:31.258
<i>They're such humble evolutions.</i>

17:32.593 --> 17:33.510
<i>It can be done.</i>

17:33.594 --> 17:36.805
<i>Like this. No! Like this. No!</i>

17:38.432 --> 17:39.266
<i>Like this!</i>

17:40.434 --> 17:41.310
<i>This is it!</i>

17:49.610 --> 17:51.653
There you are.

17:51.737 --> 17:55.407
I have nothing but gratitude
for your rushing here

17:55.491 --> 17:57.409
for my foolish son, Katsumi.

17:57.493 --> 17:58.827
Foolish son?

17:59.828 --> 18:01.246
Not at all.

18:03.082 --> 18:03.916
Retsu.

18:05.000 --> 18:08.504
I heard you once defeated that kid
with a single blow.

18:09.922 --> 18:12.633
Unfortunately, that's the truth.

18:13.759 --> 18:16.428
Yet I find that hard to believe.

18:20.432 --> 18:21.725
That was in the past.

18:22.226 --> 18:24.436
Katsumi is a changed man now.

18:24.520 --> 18:27.189
How would it turn out now?

18:28.774 --> 18:31.443
I'm not sure. Now, well...

18:31.527 --> 18:35.989
If the genius and master fighter
Sea King Retsu acknowledges his skill,

18:36.073 --> 18:40.202
then the natural genius
of Katsumi Orochi must be quite powerful.

18:42.412 --> 18:43.705
I don't disagree.

18:44.331 --> 18:47.709
The new punch I taught him the other day,

18:48.293 --> 18:50.921
he's probably already mastered it.

18:51.004 --> 18:52.464
And in fact...

18:56.552 --> 19:01.682
by now, he's surpassed it by far.

19:03.267 --> 19:06.145
<i>This is it. I can feel it now.</i>

19:06.228 --> 19:08.188
<i>My preparations are complete.</i>

19:08.939 --> 19:12.860
<i>To throw the greatest punch,
this stance is necessary.</i>

19:13.443 --> 19:15.362
<i>In every corner of my body,</i>

19:15.445 --> 19:17.322
<i>I must be as loose as mush.</i>

19:17.948 --> 19:19.783
<i>As loose as mush,</i>

19:20.450 --> 19:22.161
<i>and prepared for the opportunity.</i>

19:23.704 --> 19:28.000
<i>I must reject that my fist
is even a weapon at all.</i>

19:28.083 --> 19:30.878
<i>Hold it so it is neither gripped nor open.</i>

19:31.461 --> 19:34.840
<i>The not-gripped-nor-opened pose
from that time at the start of life</i>

19:34.923 --> 19:37.634
<i>when the hands were first formed.</i>

19:38.427 --> 19:40.637
<i>And my image of the joints...</i>

19:43.974 --> 19:45.100
<i>is like this.</i>

19:47.644 --> 19:49.897
<i>Even I am trembling.</i>

19:49.980 --> 19:53.108
<i>I'm just letting a punch loose
in an empty space.</i>

19:53.192 --> 19:57.654
<i>Yet I'm trembling before making
such an ordinary move in a dojo.</i>

19:58.238 --> 20:00.407
<i>That sensation I felt in my hand.</i>

20:01.033 --> 20:03.911
<i>That image of moving
only what's beyond the shoulder.</i>

20:04.494 --> 20:05.913
<i>With all my body.</i>

20:05.996 --> 20:07.372
<i>With all my might.</i>

20:28.518 --> 20:30.938
Ch... Chairman...

20:31.772 --> 20:35.275
Hey, Terada. It's pretty awesome

20:35.359 --> 20:38.445
when you master even just one thing.

20:39.029 --> 20:42.449
What the heck did you just master?

20:43.033 --> 20:45.118
A killer move. A new one.

20:45.786 --> 20:47.454
And you've mastered it?

20:51.416 --> 20:52.960
Hey, quit pushing, dang it!

20:54.586 --> 20:55.963
Yeah, you could say that.

20:57.130 --> 20:58.757
<i>Have I mastered it?</i>

20:59.341 --> 21:01.468
<i>That feeling, it's quite mysterious.</i>

21:02.094 --> 21:04.972
<i>I never imagined it would feel like that.</i>

21:11.561 --> 21:14.356
Rumina, did you hear that just now?

21:15.607 --> 21:18.485
No. Was it some sound? Or a voice?

21:18.568 --> 21:20.570
No, never mind.

21:21.571 --> 21:24.491
So, who are you fighting?

21:24.574 --> 21:26.743
They'll be here soon.

21:27.327 --> 21:29.788
<i>That's probably what it was.
I've gotta hurry now.</i>

21:35.627 --> 21:37.004
Are you fighting Strydum?!

21:37.671 --> 21:38.588
Hello.

21:44.303 --> 21:46.305
I don't see anyone here.

21:47.055 --> 21:48.765
Who are you gonna fight?

21:50.309 --> 21:51.685
They'll show up now.

22:00.610 --> 22:03.280
<i>I know what it is. He's imagining it.</i>

22:06.867 --> 22:08.785
You two, back up.

22:09.369 --> 22:13.123
<i>At this time, the only one
who knew of his opponent...</i>

22:14.583 --> 22:16.293
What? It's gigantic!

22:16.960 --> 22:18.879
<i>...was Baki himself.</i>
